  "scope": "# Registered natural-chain continuation pilot\n\nThis executes the previously published prospective pilot without changing its\n200-update base endpoints,0.001 peak rate,0.3 answer/0.03 EOS loss weights,\n128 NTP windows plus applicable128 tasks per update,curriculum quarters or\none-pass versus4/1/2 full-gradient depth schedule. It is a one-pair development\ncontinuation,not the original from-scratch/general-text success criterion.\n\nAll conditions start from the original completed One/NTP seed5231 body at\n1.004887590B natural targets. Reset optimizers identically. No fitted driver-\nqualification weights enter the pilot. Continue the original natural source\nstream at window1920*512 without wrapping. The paired order of new NTP windows\nis identical across conditions. Source-task examples use a frozen shuffled\nproblem stream;all views of a problem are one example,not independent data.\nTask latent noise varies by exposure and is independent of task identity or\nanswer. No teacher-model,numerical answer generation,RL or new architecture.\n\nCases are One/NTP,One/bridge,R/NTP,R/bridge,plus One/bridge-work. One's head,\nparameter inventory and cheap recurrent adapter machinery match R exactly;\nonly repeated applications differ. Retain all applicable128-position task\nmatmuls,1024-position NTP matmuls,full backward paths,vocabulary projections and\nall32 replicated optimizer matrix updates in the nominal-work ledger. The\nlonger One endpoint is the greatest whole-update count that does not exceed\nR/bridge's200-update incremental budget;require shortfall below1%. It has its\nown curriculum and completed cooldown. Its first stable update may branch from\nOne/bridge only because that update's data,depth,objective,rate and optimizer\nare exactly identical. No cooled checkpoint is extended.\n\n## Execution and integration\n\nFreeze exact source lists,all data/tokenizer/noise/sampler hashes,counts,work\ncontrol endpoint,readout exits and resource limits before the first update.\nFirst execute one actual registered update per basic case,save its full state\nand global raw gradient,and stop. Count those updates as research even if a\nlater gate fails. Require independent pinned upstream FP32 gradients for every\none of the128 NTP windows and applicable128 source-task answers,all parameter\nfamilies within2%,component NLL differences within0.003,and independent\nobserved-gradient clipping/optimizer/moment agreement. All32 replicas must agree.\nNo further update until its complete integration gate passes.\n\nEvery continuation must restore exact model/optimizer/per-rank RNG state and\nthe same source/task/work counters. Record any future-trajectory differences;\nno guarantee of bit-exact native future training is asserted. Each200-update\nbase arm gets10 warmup updates,stable rate through100,and cosine cooldown to\n10% of peak. Longer One retains the common10-update warmup and scales its own\nhalf-endpoint cooldown/curriculum. Measure100 actual mixed warm updates20\u2013119.\nThis finite pilot precedes larger training;there is no HPO in either arm.\n\nA conservative measured feasibility bound combines the already qualified\nbatch-one1024-position NTP update and128-position task timings. Allocate at most\n2s per mixed update after warmup,plus900s for each launch/capture/restore and\nup to1,200s per CPU audit. The overall fixed execution cap is7,200s;native phase\ncap1,200s;CPU phase cap1,200s. Stop at a failed numerical prerequisite/resource\ncap,not an unfavorable scientific outcome. Do not change endpoints or grant an\nextension after seeing quality. Use both eight-chip halves when ready,with owned\nworker cleanup. Preserve512GiB host MemAvailable and35GiB free per output FS.\nCount compilation,all launches/failed attempts,repeated tasks and CPU tails.\n\n## Frozen readouts\n\nOnly after all fits,score all five checkpoints on the existing135-task/115-group\nconsumed discovery DEV. One uses depth1;R reports1,2,4 with depth2 declared as its\nprimary operating point. Use the exact baseline's prefix-only/no-work view,\n24-token greedy budget,EOS requirement and whole-scalar verifier. Reuse the same\nprefix-derived latent noise. No best-depth selection. Independently audit every\nfull-panel answer NLL with the pinned upstream FP32 model. All source strings,\ntokens,predictions and states remain private.\n\nPrimary domain pilot contrast is R/bridge depth2 minus One/bridge depth1 in\nwhole-answer accuracy. Report the factorial interaction,same-R depth1\u21922 change,\nR/bridge versus the longer One/bridge-work control,and all secondary exits.\nUse the predeclared5pp interesting-effect screen;report conditional paired\nsource-group bootstrap intervals separately from unavailable seed uncertainty.\nA one-pair development result cannot establish statistical replication. The\noriginal0.01-nat broad-natural-source useful-gain rule is unchanged.\n\nAlso score every endpoint on the common consumed natural-text DEV curve cohort,\nat the declared default depth,using independent FP32 source-token NLL and the\nsame60/20/20 weights. Compare curriculum retention with its respective NTP-only\ncase. Report any degradation;do not substitute arithmetic accuracy for broad\nprediction. The shared original pretraining cost belongs to every conceptual\nmodel comparison;actual campaign receipts count only executed additional work.\nNominal matched work does not mean matched chip-hours or serving cost.\n\nThis pilot does not include a tuned textual-scratchpad challenger,independent\nnew training seeds,full from-scratch curriculum or terminal TEST. A favorable\nresult still needs stronger equally tuned baselines,replicated fresh training,\nappropriate inference-cost controls and the charter's independent confirmation.\nA null/negative result stays in the record. No automatic larger run,threshold\nchange,new objective weight/depth or favorable-subset search follows.\n",
